<title>USA: Sequa says judge declines relief to Pratt.</title>
<headline>Sequa says judge declines relief to Pratt.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sequa Corp said Tuesday a judge refused to award relief on the counterclaims of the Pratt &amp; Whitney division of United Technologies Corp an antitrust case brought by Sequa's Chromalloy Gas Turbine Corp unit.</p>
<p>Sequa said that Texas State Court Judge John Specia ruled the company's actions resulted in no injury to Pratt, and he declined to award any of the relief which Pratt was seeking.</p>
<p>The company also said the judge confirmed a lower court decision to deny Chromalloy's motion for injunctive relief based on a jury's antitrust verdict against Pratt.</p>
</text>
